      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T18:42:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, right, didn\u0027t realize you needed it to be mutated and also to send over D-Bus.\n\nIn that case, some recommendations:\n* prefer that we copy the things that eventually will be moved anyway, which are the adv_id and the params.\n* prefer to iterate the elements directly rather than the iterate the keys and then use the keys to index (more efficient).\n* `self.context.lock().unwrap()` is used multiple times in the vicinity we can acquire the lock once and use it for subsequent operations.\n\n```\n# Acquire once for conciseness.\n# It\u0027s safe since the lock will be released right after the end of the block.\nlet mut context \u003d self.context.lock().unwrap();\n\n# Mutable operation can be separated on its own. For loop is okay too but I think\n# `Iterator::for_each` is suitable in this case.\ncontext.adv_sets.iter_mut().for_each(|(_, set)| set.params.interval \u003d interval);\n\n# Immutable operation, and also collecting what needs to be sent over D-Bus.\n# Cloning is okay since we need to avoid deadlock and the data will be moved when\n# calling D-Bus anyway.\nlet advs: Vec\u003c(_, _)\u003e \u003d context\n    .adv_sets\n    .iter()\n    .filter_map(|(_reg_id, set)| {\n        set.adv_id.map(|adv_id| (adv_id.clone(), set.params.clone()))\n    })\n    .collect();\n\n# Just sending the cloned data to D-Bus.\nfor (adv_id, params) in advs {\n    print_info!(\"Setting advertising parameters for {}\", adv_id);\n    context.gatt_dbus.as_mut().unwrap().set_advertising_parameters(adv_id, params);\n}\n\n```\n\nCan you try to apply similar pattern to the other similar situation above?",
